 ## Next release and retirement gates
 
-* Deploy this 7.0 reader everywhere first. Then promote the tested 7.2 lock,
-  change `load_defaults` to 7.2 and keep the scoped mail metadata and cache
-  overrides above. The old `secrets.yml` API is gone in 7.2: if in use, move
-  the **same effective value** to a supported secret source before switching.
-  Check precedence if more than one source is configured.
-* Keep the SHA1 mail reader until at least 30 days after the **last** old
-  sender (including queued jobs and any rollback). Keep old cookie readers
-  and `:hybrid` until no valid old sessions can return; if lifetime is
-  unbounded, do not remove them on a calendar deadline. Keep support for
-  Marshal mail until the last such link expires. Do not address any of these
-  transitions by accepting unsigned cookies or links.
-* Once **7.0 is no longer a rollback target**, 7.2 can use its new metadata
-  envelope and cache/record formats. The new Rails reader also understands
-  old envelopes. Retire the staged compatibility branches and move the
-  writer assertions to the newly supported release pair at that point.
-* Rails 7.2 defaults no longer supply a coder for bare `serialize`. The
-  preview explicitly retains YAML for existing columns; make remaining core
-  and plugin coders/types explicit before removing that setting. Audit plugins
-  for nested session data, required `belongs_to`, formatted `to_s`, redirects,
-  migration APIs, and 7.2 transaction/job callback timing. Rehearse migrations
-  and shared caches with the production adapter, not just SQLite.
+* Deploy this reader everywhere first. Once **7.2 is the rollback floor**,
+  promote the 8.1 lock, `load_defaults 8.1`, remove the scoped legacy metadata
+  writer option and both cache/record format pins. Keep the named verifier's
+  old-key reader. Move writer assertions to the new formats. Do not roll back
+  past 7.2 once 8.1 has emitted new envelopes/records. Audit 8.1 redirect,
+  JSON escaping, form rendering and finder ordering defaults with site plugins.
+* Read rotations have a different retirement gate than writer overrides.
+  Retain the SHA1 mail key and support for Marshal mail until at least 30 days
+  after the **last** corresponding sender (including queued jobs and rollbacks).
+  Keep the old cookie keys and `:hybrid` until no still-valid old session can
+  return. If lifetime is unbounded there is no safe calendar cutoff. Do not
+  weaken signature, purpose, expiry or DB session checks during retirement.
